The Philippines has been hit by a series of tropical weather systems this month, intensifying the Southwest Monsoon and bringing widespread flooding. Now, Tropical Storm Eleven (known locally as “Emong”) is expected to make landfall over Northern Luzon within the next 24-48 hours, bringing damaging winds and heavy rains that could trigger additional floods and landslides.

The first screenshot highlights PDC’s latest Event Brief, which estimates that approximately 1.64 Million people (397,000 households) may be exposed to damaging winds along the forecast path. Event Briefs are automatically updated with each new advisory, providing actionable information to support rapid response and informed decision-making.

The second screenshot displays the Precipitation Forecast layer in DisasterAWARE, highlighting the potential accumulated rainfall amounts across the area for the next 10 days.

